# No `void` Operator

Do not use the JavaScript `void` operator. That includes silencing floating promises with `void someAsync()`.

Return-type annotations like `: void` on functions that return nothing are fine.

## Prefer

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — async handler, await the work
async function onSubmit(event: FormEvent<HTMLFormElement>) {
  event.preventDefault();
  const response = await login({ email, password });
  // ...
}

// ✅ GOOD — sync callback that must return void: attach handlers
onClick={() => {
  fetchNextPage().catch(error => {
    console.error(error);
  });
}}

// ✅ GOOD — type annotation
function reset(): void {
  setValue('');
}
```

## Avoid

```ts
// ❌ BAD
void login({ email, password }).then(...);
void fetchNextPage();
void setFilters({ sort: value });
onClick={() => void handleRedeem()};
```

## Rules

- New and edited code must not introduce `void expr`.
- Do not “mark” floating promises with `void`; await them in an `async` function, or handle rejection with `.catch` / `try/catch`.
- Do not mass-rewrite unrelated existing `void` call sites unless the task already touches those lines.
